data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 10, the Cosmos DB provider already **threw by default** on synchronous LINQ operations, but you could suppress it:

```csharp
options.ConfigureWarnings(w =>
    w.Ignore(CosmosEventId.SyncNotSupported));
```

In **.NET 11 (EF Core 11)**, that opt-in is **removed entirely**. The sync-over-async code path is gone from the Cosmos provider. Every synchronous call in your repository — `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()` — will **fail to compile or throw `InvalidOperationException`** at runtime.

## Fix: convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key changes:**
1. Return `Task<T>` / `Task` instead of bare types
2. Use `ToListAsync()`, `FirstAsync()`, `CountAsync()`, `SaveChangesAsync()`
3. `await` each call, mark methods `async`
4. Remove the `CosmosEventId.SyncNotSupported` suppression — it no longer exists
5. Update all callers to `await` the new async methods

This isn't Cosmos-specific advice — the relational providers still support sync — but the Cosmos SDK itself is async-only, so EF Core dropped the sync façade.
